  "46fcbbe0-f5e4-4ff4-a564-4707c4676145": {
   "id": "46fcbbe0-f5e4-4ff4-a564-4707c4676145",
   "message": {
    "id": "46fcbbe0-f5e4-4ff4-a564-4707c4676145",
    "author": {
     "role": "assistant",
     "name": null,
     "metadata": {}
    },
    "create_time": 1777867041.646,
    "update_time": null,
    "content": {
     "content_type": "text",
     "parts": [
      "It's risky. If windows from the same student appear in both train and test, models can exploit student-specific patterns and the benchmark overstates performance. A student-grouped split (all of a student's windows on one side) is the standard fix.\n\nIf you can, switch to `GroupShuffleSplit` by `student_id` before Wednesday and report that. If you truly can't rerun everything in time, at minimum say in the datasheet that the current split is window-level and that a grouped split is planned. A careful reviewer will spot it otherwise."
     ]
    },
    "status": "finished_successfully",
